Permission for evaluation
-------------------------
Anyone may read, download, run and test this repository to evaluate or review
it, including Smart India Hackathon evaluators and the Narcotics Control Bureau.
No other right is granted. Copying, modifying, redistributing, or using this
code or its documents in a product or service requires written permission from
the team.

Why this is not yet an open-source licence
------------------------------------------
Under the SIH 2026 guidelines, the intellectual property of a winning idea is
split between the organisation that set the problem statement (here the
Narcotics Control Bureau, MHA) and the team, or is decided by mutual agreement.
Granting an irrevocable open-source licence now would pre-empt that agreement.
The intended outcome is government ownership with open record formats (see
README.md); the final licence will be agreed with NCB.

Third-party material
--------------------
Third-party software, certificates and data used by this repository keep their
own licences and terms. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.

No warranty; not for evidential use
-----------------------------------
THE SOFTWARE IS PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED. It is a research prototype. All signing keys in this repository are
test keys, colour results are from simulated photos, and every result is
presumptive only. It must not be used to record real seizures.
